{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793912207,"nonce":"iiBX5pFCsSQemxQ8Wf8+RMpyV94=","message":"The collector cold-helper experiment is withheld; no commit or local source change.\n\nCandidate over 6d9f9ba3 only moves large_block/large marking into a cold, non-inlined helper. It excludes the withheld inliner candidate and the subsequently landed function-order correction. Existing large-block reachability and pool-cursor GC tests pass on the NUC. No full local conformance/corpus run was claimed for this unlanded experiment.\n\n378 normal LLVM-off, default-tiered, snapshot-enabled wall samples: 21 alternating pairs across 9 cases. Frozen binaries, no cargo/rustc during samples, guarded affinity/load/temperature/throttle, all PUC Lua 5.4 reference outputs pass. Before/after wall medians in ms: method_call 27.593/27.257; op_overload 32.099/31.493; binary_trees 144.559/145.130; records 81.855/81.310; pipeline 321.482/319.987; tokenize 103.678/106.209; collatz 142.027/140.799; method_short 18.890/18.589; method_long 45.109/44.512. Paired ratios and exploratory bootstrap intervals are in analysis.json. Tokenize ratio is 1.01928, interval 1.00999..1.03404. The intended kernel did not improve, so no further wall-control batch was needed to accept this candidate: it is rejected, with no claim that the source change's causal slowdown is fully established.\n\nSeven alternating instrumented GC pairs confirm snapshot placement and exactly two collections in both arms. Carved KB and freed-block counts match (32817/39299 KB, 225231/464434 blocks); live/heap totals differ by at most 2 KB. Summed mark medians 15.53 -\u003e 17.31 ms; total collection 16.84 -\u003e 18.71 ms. Raw phase traces retained. Assembly confirms the intended outlining happened: consider shrinks from 1192 to 607 bytes; consider_large is 788 bytes. A smaller hot function alone did not produce a marking or wall-time gain. Do not describe